# Local overrides for `docker compose`. Copy this file to `.env` (already
# gitignored) and edit as needed — `docker compose` reads `.env` from the
# project root automatically, no `--env-file` flag required.
#
# Every variable below already has a working default baked into
# docker-compose.yml, so an unmodified `.env` (or no `.env` at all) is a
# valid starting point: `make quickstart` / `docker compose up` runs the
# rules-only stack with nothing set here. Uncomment and edit only the knobs
# you actually want to change.
#
# Variables NOT listed here (ARMOR_AUTH_MODE, ARMOR_RATE_LIMIT_MODE,
# ARMOR_BIND_ADDR, RUST_LOG, ARMOR_INFERENCE_PROFILE, ...) are set directly
# in docker-compose.yml's `environment:` blocks rather than sourced from
# the shell/.env — see the inline comments next to each in that file for
# what they do and how to flip them.

# --- ML tier -----------------------------------------------------------
# Points armor-core at the inference sidecar. Leave unset/empty to stay
# in rules-only mode even with `--profile ml` running. `make ml-up` sets
# this for you; only needed here if you start the `ml` profile by hand.
# Safe to leave set even when the `ml` profile isn't running: armor-api logs
# a warning and starts rules-only rather than failing to start, and the
# control-plane UI reports the sidecar as unreachable until it comes up.
# ARMOR_INFERENCE_URL=http://inference:9000

# Shared secret between armor-core and the inference sidecar. Must match on
# both — set once here and it applies to both services. `make ml-up`
# generates one into this file for you the first time it runs (skip this
# line entirely if you use that); only set it by hand if you're starting
# the `ml` profile with plain `docker compose` and want a stable token
# across restarts instead of `make`'s generated one. Without *some* token,
# POST /api/v1/models/install (and /reload) always 401s — the sidecar never
# leaves those endpoints unauthenticated, even with nothing configured (see
# inference/README.md).
# ARMOR_INFERENCE_AUTH_TOKEN=devtoken

# Where the inference sidecar's model weights live on the host. Default is
# a managed Docker volume (survives `docker compose down`, not visible as a
# host path). Point this at a local directory instead if you want to
# inspect/reuse downloaded weights directly, e.g. ./models
# ARMOR_MODELS_DIR=./models

# HuggingFace access token, forwarded as-is to the `inference` and
# `ml-fetch` services (huggingface_hub reads this env var itself for every
# download/export call). Only needed if you've pinned a candidate model that
# is gated on the Hub, e.g. vijil/mbert-prompt-injection — get one at
# https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens after requesting/accepting access
# to the gated repo itself. Every catalog default is a public repo and needs
# none of this.
# HF_TOKEN=hf_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Per-call / whole-escalation-pass deadlines from armor-core to the
# sidecar. Already bumped in docker-compose.yml (2000ms / 3000ms) from the
# binary's own built-in defaults (120ms / 250ms) because those are sized
# for server/GPU-class hardware — real (non-stub) catalog models on a
# CPU-only box routinely take 85-540ms solo and more under concurrent
# escalation. Raise further on a slower
# CPU, or drop back toward the binary defaults once running on hardware
# that comfortably beats them.
# ARMOR_INFERENCE_TIMEOUT_MS=2000
# ARMOR_INFERENCE_BUDGET_MS=3000
